    "created_at": "2016-02-29T08:39:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-29T08:39:44Z",
    "body": "Or what would make more sense, and fit with the extensible web ethos of low level APIs first, is accepting an object for `timeout` allowing numerous timeouts to be specified\n\ne.g.\n\n``` js\ntimeout: {\n   firstByte: 700,\n   headers: 1000,\n   fullContent: 2000,\n   interPackage: 50\n}\n```\n\nwith `timeout: 2000` being an alias for `timeout: {content: 2000}`\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
