    "created_at": "2016-07-17T22:16:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-17T22:16:47Z",
    "body": "The lack of some way to set reasonable timeouts makes this API unusable for Cordova based mobile apps. Users expect their apps to respond in a reasonable time and we need to be able to control this. \n\nYes you can use settimeout and then ignore the request but leaving a no longer useful connection open in the background that may waste data is not acceptable for a mobile app where connectivity is potentially flaky, especially if you want to limit the number of connections to your API. \n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
